        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Mali faces 'very high risk' of new coup d'état, analyst says, amid jihadist insurgence Africa Issued on: 29/04/2026 - 21:37 Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Michael Shurkin, Director of Global Programmes at 14 North Strategies, says that Mali faces a very high risk of a new coup d'état, adding that the jihadist group JNIM and the Tuareg rebels of the FLA \"clearly have the initiative and the Malian government is on the backfoot\". Tuareg rebels urge Russian forces to leave Mali 29/04/2026 Africa 'Over-dependence on military solutions: Mali struggling in its effort to regain peace and security' 29/04/2026 MALI Insurgents reshaping Mali: Tuaregs seek autonomy, jihadists pursue caliphate across Sahel 28/04/2026 MALI Mali capital 'not under threat, but long-term prospects do not look good', analyst says 28/04/2026 Africa Mali's tale of two insurgencies: 'Jihadists seek caliphate while Tuareg rebels pursue autonomy' 27/04/2026 Africa 'Unable to cope': Malian army, Wagner 'overstretched' by Tuareg separatists and jihadist militants 27/04/2026 Africa Russian mercenaries in Mali: Limited gains, reports of abuse 26/04/2026 Africa Malian Defence Minister Sadio Camara killed by rebels 26/04/2026 Africa Gunfire and blasts rock Mali: Army claims situation is under control 26/04/2026 Africa"
